Who wants it? → Business Owner / Product / Growth / Sponsor
Who approves or funds it? → Executive Sponsor / Finance / relevant decision authority
Who provides evidence? → Data / Analytics
Who uses or is affected by it? → End Users
Who designs it? → UX/UI
Who builds it? → Engineering / Development
Who tests it? → QA / Testing
Who constrains or regulates it? → Legal / Compliance / Data Privacy
Who connects and translates these needs into requirements? → Business Analyst. 
Identified 9 stakeholder teams.

R — Responsible: actually performs the work.
A — Accountable: ultimately owns the outcome/decision. Ideally one A per activity.
C — Consulted: provides input before/during the work; two-way communication.
I — Informed: needs to know what happened; mostly one-way communication.

In a situation where a Growth Manager puts ahead a situation like:
Growth Manager: “I want a widget like Duolingo that urges users to track daily.”

R:Developers        
A: Growth/Product Manager
C: UI/UX               
I:C-suite           
